{"parentUuid":"613ecdf8-afe5-4dd9-ae8d-1a58f3d02236","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb45681e-01fe-49eb-ac32-0d9fce8ec22d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wh6fX5MVMyvSNUxntjzCqz","type":"tool_result","content":"Location: crates/core/src/extractor/factory_props.rs:55-59\n\nFor a factory returning `React.FC<{ id?: string }>`, a render callback such as `({ size = 'M' }: { size?: 'S' | 'M' }) => <div />` now contributes `size`, but its default remains absent. This path captures only the annotation; unlike normal function extraction, it never calls `extract_param_defaults`, and the body-default walker does not capture parameter defaults. Collect and attach those defaults alongside the callback props.\n\nLocation: crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs:654-656\n\nAfter a lazy session resolves `Button`, editing only a consumer’s JSX can change `Button`’s `used` list here without reporting it in `updated_keys`. `next_lazy` retains that resolution without marking it touched (lines 299–309), and `lazy_delta` reports only touched names (lines 384–387), so clients relying on update notifications retain stale relevance data. Compare call-site evidence for retained lazy answers and include affected keys in the delta.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9c8b6c8f-9c42-4292-a7a6-ef91264902b3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T05:48:48.497Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Location: crates/core/src/extractor/factory_props.rs:55-59\n\nFor a factory returning `React.FC<{ id?: string }>`, a render callback such as `({ size = 'M' }: { size?: 'S' | 'M' }) => <div />` now contributes `size`, but its default remains absent. This path captures only the annotation; unlike normal function extraction, it never calls `extract_param_defaults`, and the body-default walker does not capture parameter defaults. Collect and attach those defaults alongside the callback props.\n\nLocation: crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs:654-656\n\nAfter a lazy session resolves `Button`, editing only a consumer’s JSX can change `Button`’s `used` list here without reporting it in `updated_keys`. `next_lazy` retains that resolution without marking it touched (lines 299–309), and `lazy_delta` reports only touched names (lines 384–387), so clients relying on update notifications retain stale relevance data. Compare call-site evidence for retained lazy answers and include affected keys in the delta.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ed94785e-19f0-40d1-9443-ee1b8a8c9eaa","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf5-483","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"613ecdf8-afe5-4dd9-ae8d-1a58f3d02236","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf5-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
