trail finding show 01M7HDCRWP08 --branch feat/relevance-output --repo gh/orin-dx/caliper --project gh/orin-dx` and crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs (~290-310 `next_lazy`, ~380-390 `lazy_delta`, ~654-656), revision.rs (the eager path already reports components whose layers/`used` changed through call sites: reuse that rule, one owner), relevance/mod.rs `apply`. The finding: after a lazy session resolves `Button`, editing only a CONSUMER's JSX can change Button's `used` list without it appearing in `updated_keys`, because `next_lazy` keeps the retained resolution without marking it touched and `lazy_delta` reports only touched names; clients that rely on update notifications keep stale relevance data. Fix: for retained lazy answers, compare the relevance-bearing result (the `used` lists/relevance evidence) against the new revision's call-site evidence and include the affected keys in the delta, using the same comparison the eager path uses (do not write a second rule). Known context: an earlier parked branch tried this (commit 7137bf80, local only, in /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a518d0c89389edba6; `git log` may show it): read it for ideas, do not copy blindly. Tests first (fail on base) in the watch/lazy model test (crates/core/tests/relevance_watch_model.rs): add an edit kind 'edit only a consumer's JSX' (add/remove `<Button className>` in another file) after a lazy resolution, and assert the lazy delta's updated keys include Button when its `used` changed and do NOT include unaffected components; also an import-only edit kind (consumer's import changes which tag is Button). Mutation proof: removing your comparison makes the model fail. Gates (targeted): `pnpm install --offline --ignore-scripts --frozen-lockfile` in the worktree first; `just lint doc-check machete typos`; nextest `-p caliper-docgen-core -p caliper-docgen-semantic`; `just test-checker-lane` (symlink target/release in the worktree to your CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release); report watch edit refresh time before/after on gate-large if cheap (skip if not). Then `/code-review low` once and AWAIT its output; fix only real bugs. Own CARGO_TARGET_DIR under /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper-fixtures/shrink/, rust 1.99.1 first on PATH (/Users/gabe/.rustup/toolchains/1.99.1-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin). Cap 60 tool calls. Final message at most 50 words: branch, SHA, exit codes, mutation result.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba/tasks/a187d00923dc15ff1.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"dcd2ec89-5ec3-4b4c-b756-840e7e82ec10","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","branch":"mf5-483","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81d9d7dc-1c66-45e4-bf89-87fd7eeaee18","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf5-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
