{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","bridgeSessionId":"cse_013R2ytvK9B32ZaSUaSe6aAZ","lastSequenceNum":15975,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"a6671d1a-1df2-4cd7-a239-870fa5394c34","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch65iKZAA5DesPR4n3bR1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two workers are fixing the two open findings. Neither pushes, and I'll push and resolve when each reports.\n\n**Change 278 (#480): factory callback defaults** (Sonnet, 40 calls)\n- **The finding:** a render callback like `({ size = 'M' }: { size?: 'S' | 'M' }) => <div />` now contributes `size`, but its default is absent, because the factory path never calls `extract_param_defaults`.\n- **The fix:** collect the callback's destructuring defaults with the same function normal components use, and attach them to the callback's props.\n- **Tests, failing first:**\n  - The finding's example gives `defaultValue` `'M'`.\n  - A callback with no default gives none.\n  - The allow-list from my last fix still holds.\n  - A nested, renamed or computed-key destructure is skipped and never guessed.\n\n**Change 281 (#483): stale `used` in the lazy delta** (Opus, 60 calls)\n- **The finding:** after a lazy session resolves `Button`, editing only a consumer's JSX can change Button's `used` list without it appearing in `updated_keys`. Clients that rely on update notifications keep stale relevance data.\n- **The fix:** compare the relevance result of retained lazy answers against the new revision's call-site evidence and include affected keys in the delta. It must reuse the eager path's rule, so there's one owner.\n- **Tests, failing first:**\n  - The watch and lazy model gets two new edit kinds: a consumer-JSX-only edit and an import-only edit.\n  - It asserts the delta includes Button when its `used` changed and excludes unaffected components.\n  - It includes a mutation proof.\n\nI told the worker about my parked T7b branch, which tried this once, to read for ideas and not copy.\n\n**Merge order is unchanged:** #480, then #483. Both are blocked on these two findings only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6521,"cache_read_input_tokens":638440,"output_tokens":621,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6521,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":621,"cache_read_input_tokens":638440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6521},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d0f3138a-ef9a-457e-ac8a-4b79eecafbe9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch65iKEouF6DcZyqsKMes","requestRef":"14019c71-323e-4a73-bd63-5f0665c6263a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fbdbfe1e-ff39-4163-b069-d072a424a248","timestamp":"2026-11-16T05:49:10.976Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abdd35c983e9e5db8","sessionId":"ad4b3461-bb6f-49f0-bb4d-997d9b8887ba","version":"2.1.311","gitBranch":"mf5-483","slug":"hazy-conjuring-volcano"}
